			"notes": "## DRT 1.0.11\n\nKuudra fixes and other fixes\n\n## Kuudra\n- Key costs are now read directly from the Mage Shop and Barbarian Shop for Basic through Infernal\n- Key prices include your own discounts like emissary reputation and Seal of the Family\n- Tiers you haven't seen in the shop yet still use the old reputation-based estimate\n- Your Kuudra pet perk now increases Crimson Essence value\n- Added a new Essence shards +N% setting for extra Crimson Essence value (`/drt config`)\n- Essence amounts with commas like 2,500 now parse properly\n- Basic Kuudra chests are no longer counted as Hot\n- Plain Kuudra reward chat lines without a header are now read as loot\n- Free chests containing only Crimson Essence no longer trigger a false flag\n\n## Chest tracking fixes\n- Chests that fail to open are no longer logged\n- Open cost is recorded correctly again instead of being saved as 0\n- If the price feed briefly misses bazaar or auction data, the previous prices are kept instead of items dropping to 0 value\n- Normal storage like island chests, ender chests, backpacks and minions no longer shows the reward chest overlay or gets read as loot\n\n## Loot history\n- Value, cost and profit in the loot list now use current prices and current key costs instead of the values saved when the chest was opened\n- Added `/drt debug reprice` to update the saved values of old chest records\n- You can also use `reprice <chest number>` to reprice a single chest\n\n## Update notice\n- DRT now checks for updates when you join\n- The update message can tell you if DRT or BetterPV is outdated\n- Added a `[Get new update]` button\n- The message also includes a `Join the discord!` link\n\n## Other changes\n- Version bumped to 1.0.11\n- Builds are now only made for 26.1.2 and 26.2"
		},
